---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

export const prerender = true
---

<BaseLayout
  title="OpenEden RWA Intelligence Suite"
  description="Institutional-grade competitive analysis, on-chain velocity research, and USDO supply cohort modeling for OpenEden’s RWA protocol suite (PRISM + USDO)."
  ogType="article"
>
  <div class="case-layout">
    <article class="case-container">
      <header class="case-header">
        <a href="/projects" class="back-link">← Projects</a>
        <h1 class="case-title">OpenEden RWA Intelligence Suite</h1>
        <p class="case-subtitle">
          A consulting engagement producing three research modules for OpenEden’s RWA products: <strong>PRISM</strong>,
          <strong>USDO</strong>, and <strong>TBILL</strong> — with reproducible pipelines, charts, and test coverage.
        </p>

        <div class="meta-row">
          <span class="meta-pill">Consulting</span>
          <span class="meta-sep">•</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Python</span>
          <span class="meta-sep">•</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">pandas</span>
          <span class="meta-sep">•</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Reproducible reports</span>
          <span class="meta-sep">•</span>
          <time class="meta-pill" datetime="2026-02-27">Feb 27, 2026</time>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="kicker">
        <div class="kicker-item">
          <span class="kicker-label">Problem</span>
          <span class="kicker-value">
            OpenEden needed <strong>institutional-grade</strong> clarity on competitive positioning, real usage (velocity)
            in XRPL vs Ethereum, and the structural drivers behind USDO supply drawdowns — in a form that could be
            validated, reproduced, and handed off.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="kicker-item">
          <span class="kicker-label">Solution</span>
          <span class="kicker-value">
            Shipped a 3-module intelligence suite: (1) competitive landscape + objection handling, (2) on-chain velocity
            + chain prioritization + 90-day actions, (3) supply cohort modeling with scenario planning and cohort-flow
            artifacts — backed by cached raw data, analysis scripts, and unit tests.
          </span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="content">
        <h2>What shipped</h2>
        <div class="deliverables">
          <div class="deliverable-card">
            <h3>Module 1 — Competitive Landscape</h3>
            <p>
              Competitive matrix for PRISM vs tokenized yield peers (Ondo, Maple, Superstate, Hamilton Lane), plus a
              differentiated value prop and an investor objection handler with explicit confidence levels and sourcing.
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Outputs</strong>: Competitive matrix, self-critique of apples-to-oranges comparisons</li>
              <li><strong>Decision utility</strong>: What’s knowable today vs what’s undisclosed / needs verification</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="deliverable-card">
            <h3>Module 2 — On-chain Velocity & Holder Behavior</h3>
            <p>
              XRPL vs Ethereum TBILL activity analysis, a Doppler Finance case study, a weighted chain priority matrix
              for USDO expansion, and three concrete 90-day recommendations to move XRPL from “storage” to “velocity”.
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Outputs</strong>: Case study, chain scoring model, 90-day action plan</li>
              <li><strong>Key insight</strong>: a ~15,000× velocity gap (XRPL TBILL transfers vs Ethereum)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="deliverable-card">
            <h3>Module 3 — USDO Supply Scenarios & Cohort Context</h3>
            <p>
              A 12‑month bear/base/bull scenario model for USDO supply, plus a root-cause analysis of the post‑incentive
              drawdown using cohort boundaries derived from structural inflection points in the supply series.
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Outputs</strong>: Scenarios + actions, hypotheses H1/H2/H3 with explicit data gaps</li>
              <li><strong>Artifact</strong>: Cohort-flow structure for “peak → steady state” retention</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>Artifacts (charts + cohort flow)</h2>

        <figure class="figure">
          <img
            src="/images/projects/openeden/module2_chart1.png"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="Monthly transfer activity comparing XRPL and Ethereum TBILL token velocity"
          />
          <figcaption>Module 2 — Monthly transfer activity: XRPL vs Ethereum (velocity signal).</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure class="figure">
          <img
            src="/images/projects/openeden/module2_chart2.png"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="Cumulative transfer counts plotted against unique holder snapshots"
          />
          <figcaption>Module 2 — Cumulative transfers vs unique holders (activity concentration).</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure class="figure">
          <img
            src="/images/projects/openeden/module2_chart3.png"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="Estimated holder archetype breakdown by monthly transfer activity"
          />
          <figcaption>Module 2 — Holder archetypes by transfer behavior (who drives velocity).</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure class="figure">
          <div class="svg-wrap" role="img" aria-label="USDO cohort flow from peak supply to steady state with redemptions and retention">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 1200 520" width="100%" height="auto" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <defs>
                <style>
                  .node { fill: #111; opacity: 0.92; }
                  .label { font: 14px -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; fill: #111; }
                  .small { font-size: 12px; fill: #666; }
                  .flow-retention { stroke: #1f77b4; stroke-opacity: 0.55; fill: none; }
                  .flow-new { stroke: #2ca02c; stroke-opacity: 0.55; fill: none; }
                  .flow-redemption { stroke: #d62728; stroke-opacity: 0.55; fill: none; }
                </style>
              </defs>

              <!-- Columns -->
              <text x="80" y="42" class="small">Sources</text>
              <text x="420" y="42" class="small">Peak supply</text>
              <text x="740" y="42" class="small">Post-drawdown</text>
              <text x="1020" y="42" class="small">Steady state</text>

              <!-- Nodes (x, y, w, h) -->
              <rect x="70" y="110" width="22" height="72" rx="4" class="node" />
              <text x="102" y="146" class="label">Cohort A (baseline)</text>
              <text x="102" y="166" class="small">$50.1M</text>

              <rect x="70" y="215" width="22" height="356" rx="4" class="node" />
              <text x="102" y="252" class="label">New incentive capital</text>
              <text x="102" y="272" class="small">$248.7M</text>

              <rect x="410" y="110" width="22" height="428" rx="4" class="node" />
              <text x="442" y="150" class="label">Cohort B (peak)</text>
              <text x="442" y="170" class="small">$298.8M</text>

              <rect x="730" y="140" width="22" height="128" rx="4" class="node" />
              <text x="762" y="178" class="label">Cohort C</text>
              <text x="762" y="198" class="small">$89.5M retained</text>

              <rect x="730" y="286" width="22" height="300" rx="4" class="node" />
              <text x="762" y="334" class="label">Redeemed (B→C)</text>
              <text x="762" y="354" class="small">$209.3M</text>

              <rect x="1010" y="160" width="22" height="90" rx="4" class="node" />
              <text x="1042" y="195" class="label">Cohort D (steady)</text>
              <text x="1042" y="215" class="small">$63.1M</text>

              <rect x="1010" y="265" width="22" height="38" rx="4" class="node" />
              <text x="1042" y="287" class="label">Redeemed (C→D)</text>
              <text x="1042" y="307" class="small">$26.4M</text>

              <!-- Flows (stroke-width approx proportional to $) -->
              <!-- A + new capital → B -->
              <path d="M 92 146 C 190 146, 310 146, 410 146" class="flow-retention" stroke-width="10" />
              <path d="M 92 395 C 200 395, 320 395, 410 395" class="flow-new" stroke-width="50" />

              <!-- B → C + redeemed -->
              <path d="M 432 190 C 520 190, 640 190, 730 190" class="flow-retention" stroke-width="18" />
              <path d="M 432 390 C 540 390, 650 430, 730 430" class="flow-redemption" stroke-width="42" />

              <!-- C → D + redeemed -->
              <path d="M 752 204 C 840 204, 940 204, 1010 204" class="flow-retention" stroke-width="13" />
              <path d="M 752 240 C 860 260, 940 284, 1010 284" class="flow-redemption" stroke-width="5" />

              <!-- Caption note -->
              <text x="80" y="500" class="small">
                Cohort-flow diagram derived from aggregate supply data (not per-wallet). Values: DeFiLlama stablecoins API — USDO (ID 241), as of 2026‑02‑27.
              </text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <figcaption>Module 3 — Cohort flow (Sankey): peak → drawdown → steady state, with retention vs redemptions.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2>How it’s built (reproducible by design)</h2>
        <p>
          The engagement is structured like a small product: raw data is cached, transformations are test-backed, and the
          analysis produces deterministic Markdown deliverables.
        </p>

        <h3>Project structure</h3>
        <pre><code>{`openEden Consulting Project/
├── reports/                 # Final deliverables (Markdown)
├── data/                    # Cached raw + processed artifacts (timestamped)
├── src/
│   ├── collectors/          # Data ingestion (RWA.xyz, DeFiLlama, etc.)
│   ├── analytics/           # Metric computation + cohort analysis
│   └── formatters/          # PDF generation, report artifacts
└── tests/                   # Unit tests for transformations`}</code></pre>

        <h3>Runbook</h3>
        <pre><code>{`cd "openEden Consulting Project"

# Run the full pipeline (collect → analyze)
make run-all

# Run tests
make test`}</code></pre>

        <h2>Results (high-signal takeaways)</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Velocity ≠ custody</strong>: XRPL holds a large share of tokenized T‑bills but shows negligible TBILL
            transfer volume relative to Ethereum — the difference is composability and secondary-market rails.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Supply drawdowns are cohort-shaped</strong>: USDO’s post‑incentive contraction is best modeled as a
            cohort retention problem (peak → steady state retention) rather than a “single narrative” issue.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Institutional tone + explicit uncertainty</strong>: every claim is sourced or flagged with
            <code>[ASSUMPTION]</code>/<code>[DATA: as of]</code>, and low-confidence comparisons are called out directly.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .case-layout {
    display: flex;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .case-container {
    flex: 1;
    max-width: 860px;
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #666;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .case-title {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .case-subtitle {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem 0;
    color: #666;
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .meta-row {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    color: #666;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .meta-pill {
    background: #f5f5f5;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
  }

  .meta-sep {
    color: #bbb;
  }

  .kicker {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    margin: 2rem 0 3rem 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .kicker-item {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .kicker-label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: #999;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .kicker-value {
    color: #1a1a1a;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .content {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .content :global(h2) {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .content :global(h3) {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .deliverables {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem 0;
  }

  .deliverable-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .deliverable-card p {
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
    color: #333;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .deliverable-card ul {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    list-style: disc;
    color: #333;
  }

  .figure {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .figure img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .svg-wrap {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: #fff;
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: #666;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  pre {
    background-color: #f5f5f5;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .case-container {
      padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
    }

    .case-title {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }

    .content {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>

